 "cfo_summary": [
  "<strong>Total available cash is $42,522</strong> against a true bank balance of $87,522, the lowest available position in sixteen weeks. After <strong>$5,512 in external payments</strong>, projected end of week is <strong>$37,010</strong>. Ten bills, no intercompany transfers.",
  "<strong>Available cash fell $48,161 in one week</strong> on a $5,288 bill run. Countryside accounts for $68,615 of the movement, a one time loan to GRP that does not recur. Group Group took in $45,000 of park distributions on 8/21 and paid out Tim's distribution before 8/28, returning to $87. Both are explained and neither changes the forward run rate.",
  "<strong>GRP recovered fully.</strong> Available moved from negative $51,072 to positive $6,397 with no uncleared transactions, the cleanest GRP position since June. The Countryside loan funded that recovery, so the underlying pattern of GRP paying closing costs on behalf of the property entities is unchanged and will recur.",
  "<strong>Six of nine entities are below $6,600.</strong> Country Aire projects to $1,446, Decade Acres to $3,036, Riverside to $4,514, RMF to $4,620, Winterwood to $6,237 and Countryside to $5,120. Group Group sits at $87. No entity has meaningful capacity to fund another entity this week, which is a change from every prior week where Countryside was the backstop.",
  "<strong>The forecast does not go short</strong> in the nine week window, bottoming at $52,697 on 10/23. That is a better picture than last week despite the lower opening, because $45,000 of distributions have now cleared rather than sitting ahead of us. Committed watchlist spend of $20,750 lands in the first two weeks of September.",
  "<strong>Rico has been on the watchlist five weeks</strong> at $7,110 for the 44 Waterway rehab and did not appear on this run. The 8/10 review had it three quarters complete. Status needs confirming. WW:25A is new this week with $1,829 already paid through GRP and no scope on record.",
  "<strong>Two homes carry signed purchase agreements.</strong> FS2:056 is in financing with the Vincent lien to be paid from buyer loan funding rather than GRP cash. WW:6D awaits appraisal and carries a $7,000 lien to Vincent on closing. Neither has a date. Home Tracker lien amounts remain blank, so no net proceeds figure can be produced on any sale."
 ],
 "for_ownership": {
  "label": "Projected end-of-week cash",
  "number": 37010.29,
  "paragraph": "We close this week at roughly $37,000 available across all accounts after a light bill run of $5,500. Available cash dropped sharply this week, but both causes are known: Countryside made a one time loan to Golden Rule Practices to clear its overdraft, and Group Group paid out your distribution. Golden Rule Practices is now fully recovered and clean for the first time since June. The portfolio is thin across the board this week, with six of the nine accounts under $6,600, so there is no obvious source if something unexpected comes up before rent lands next week. Looking out sixty days the business covers itself without needing a home to close, though two homes are under contract and would improve the picture."
 },
